{"name":"Woven Jute","hex":"#c9ab96","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fabricated by weaving.","Interlaced"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cloth formed by weaving. It only stretches in the bias directions (between the warp and weft directions), unless the threads are elastic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woven"},{"term":"jute","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The coarse, strong fibre of the East Indian plants, Corchorus olitorius and Corchorus capsularis, used to make mats, paper, gunny cloth etc.","The plants from which this fibre is obtained."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jute"}],"entries":[{"title":"Woven fabric","blocks":[{"text":"Woven fabric is any textile formed by weaving. Woven fabrics, often created on a loom, are made of many threads woven in a warp and weft. Technically, a woven fabric is any fabric made by interlacing two or more threads at right angles to one another."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Palaung_Woman_Kalaw_Shan_Myanmar.jpg/330px-Palaung_Woman_Kalaw_Shan_Myanmar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woven_fabric"},{"title":"Jute","blocks":[{"text":"Jute is a long, rough, shiny bast fibre that can be spun into coarse, strong threads. It is produced from flowering plants in the genus Corchorus, of the mallow family Malvaceae. The primary source of the fiber is Corchorus olitorius, but such fiber is considered inferior to that derived from Corchorus capsularis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Jute_-_Kolkata_2003-10-31_00538.JPG/330px-Jute_-_Kolkata_2003-10-31_00538.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jute"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Fabr